        },
        {
            "block_label": "algorithm",
            "block_content": "Algorithm 2 One recursive step of tbtree.\n\nRequire: Node rows $\\mathcal{N}$, depth $d$, hyper-parameters $(d_{\\max}, n_{\\min}, A, B, \\tau_{\\mathrm{cv}})$, base estimator, a split objective (coskew / cov+coskew) and a leaf objective (cov), impurity, search heuristic.\n\n1: Restrict $\\mathbf{X}_{\\mathcal{N}}$, $\\mathbf{Y}_{\\mathcal{N}}$ to $\\mathcal{N}$.\n\n2: if $d \\geq d_{\\max}$ or $|\\mathcal{N}| < 2n_{\\min}$ then\n\n3: Fit the leaf model (leaf objective) on $(\\mathbf{X}_{\\mathcal{N}}, \\mathbf{Y}_{\\mathcal{N}})$ and return a leaf.\n\n4: end if\n\n5: (Optional) select per-node parameters by CV (8); record $S_{\\mathrm{p}}$ with $\\mathcal{N}$'s variance as denominator.\n\n6: Fit the split model (split objective) on $(\\mathbf{X}_{\\mathcal{N}}, \\mathbf{Y}_{\\mathcal{N}})$; compute $t_{i1}$.\n\n7: Find $\\tau^{*}$ minimizing the chosen impurity on $t_{.1}$ subject to $n_{\\min}$; if none exists, fit a leaf model and return a leaf.\n\n8: (Optional) CV gate: if $(S_{\\mathrm{p}} - S_{\\mathrm{c}})/S_{\\mathrm{p}} < \\tau_{\\mathrm{cv}}$, fit a leaf model and return a leaf.\n\n9: Recurse on the two children at depth $d + 1$.",
            "block_bbox": [
                142,
                257,
                1085,
                702
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
