        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The following study tests whether the coskewness objective helps  $ \\text{tbtree} $ recover piecewise multivariate linear regimes. A four-regime latent-variable mixture is constructed. Each regime  $ k \\in \\{1, \\ldots, 4\\} $ has an orthonormal pair of X-loadings  $ \\boldsymbol{P}_k \\in \\mathbb{R}^{p \\times 2} $ from the QR decomposition of a Gaussian matrix and a Y-loading pair  $ \\boldsymbol{Q}_k \\in \\mathbb{R}^{q \\times 2} $; the regime is centred at a Gaussian location  $ \\boldsymbol{c}_k $. With standard-Gaussian latent scores  $ \\boldsymbol{T}_k $, the rows are",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                885,
                1083,
                1030
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    885.0
                ],
                [
                    1083.0,
                    885.0
                ],
                [
                    1083.0,
                    1030.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    1030.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ \\begin{array}{r l r l r l}&{X_{k}=c_{k}+T_{k}P_{k}^{\\top}+\\sigma_{\\varepsilon}E_{x},}&{}&{Y_{k}=\\mu_{k}+T_{k}Q_{k}^{\\top}+\\sigma_{\\varepsilon}E_{y},}\\end{array} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                319,
                1050,
                902,
                1082
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    319.0,
